<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orok people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Uilta, Ulta</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Orok, who call themselves Uilta, are a small Tungusic people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakhalin">Sakhalin</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-far-east">Russian Far East</a>, numbering a few hundred. Traditionally reindeer herders, hunters and fishers, they lived in the north and east of the island. Those in southern Sakhalin came under Japanese rule in Karafuto from 1905 and were pressed to assimilate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orok-people.jpg" alt="Orok people" width="320" height="162" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uilta_People.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
